mem-project_overrun_fuelcut_tier_system.mechanism:
The two listings at 0x03AF94 are the same function, found twice by the bounds heuristic. It builds an overrun fuel-cut delay schedule. It runs only when GBR+30 (0xFFFF7C9E) is 0 (GBR = 0xFFFF7C80).

If flag 0xFFFF65C0 == 1, the base count comes from 0x0CBC9E and the stage-2/3 counts (GBR+14, GBR+16) are zeroed. Otherwise rpm_current is binned against three float thresholds: bin 0 if rpm < 2250 (0x0CC4EC), bin 1 if rpm < 3000 (0x0CC4F0), bin 2 if rpm < 4500 (0x0CC4F4), bin 3 at 4500 and above.

The bin (×4) indexes pointer tables in ROM at 0x63B70–0x63D40. The pointers lead to uint16 calibration values loaded into r4 (later GBR+12), GBR+14 and GBR+16. Which pointer-table family is used depends on three things:
- whether byte 0xFFFF5DB8 is zero (two families);
- a special case: the result of call 0x22CF4 is 0 and word 0xFFFF5E74 >= 38 (uint16 at 0x0CBCC0);
- otherwise the selector byte 0xFFFF6810 = 1, 2, 3 or 4/5, each with its own table.

If 0xFFFF8E46 == 1, the base count gets a minimum floor from 0x0CBC92. If 0xFFFF6155 == 1 and 0xFFFF615F == 0, extra offsets from 0x0C2220–0x0C2226 go into GBR+4..10 and GBR+27 is set to 1; otherwise those offsets are zeroed and GBR+27 cleared.

The final block converts the counts with fmac_interp_uint16 and forms cumulative thresholds with saturating adds:
- GBR+18 = max(GBR+12, GBR+0) + GBR+4;
- GBR+20 = that max + GBR+14 + GBR+6;
- GBR+22 = that max + GBR+14 + GBR+16 + GBR+8;
- GBR+24 = the same running sum + GBR+10.
These are staged cut-counter targets. A counter at GBR+42 is compared with GBR+18; when it has reached it, flag GBR+28 is cleared. GBR+0/GBR+28 are loaded from 0x0CBD92 only when: GBR+30 == 1, GBR+42 < GBR+18, 0xFFFF65FC >= the float at 0x0CC4F8, ECT >= the float at 0x0CC4FC, the 0x22CF4 result == 1, and 0xFFFF7EED == 1.

Separately, function 0x03ABA2 looks up the 'Overrun Fueling RPM Resume Threshold' 1-D table against ECT (fr12). It adds 0xFFFF895C and a sum of conditional float adders (held at 0xFFFF7C7C) and stores the result at 0xFFFF7C78 as the resume RPM. That value is compared with rpm_current (resume > rpm) to select a value written to 0xFFFF7C70. 0xFFFF7C6C = 0xFFFF7C70 + 0xFFFF7C74.

doc-boost-control-03.not_shown:
Values at 0x0C0BD8, 0x0C0BE8, 0x0C0BEC and 0x0C0BF4 (the integral upper limit) are not shown. The pack also does not show:
- exactly which RAM quantity 0xFFFF5C98 is (base, current or final WGDC);
- what sets 0xFFFF5CC4 or the boost error and target boost at 0xFFFF5CA0 and 0xFFFF5CA4;
- the sign convention and units of boost error;
- which boost-error axis belongs to which TD table, and the full axis contents;
- where the P and I outputs are consumed downstream, and the call rate of this routine.
